WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.580
Good morning John!  Katherine and I have been getting up at what I consider to be a sort of... evil time of the day every morning

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:10.200
for the last couple weeks, and going on a walk.

00:00:10.280 --> 00:00:15.740
I find this to be wonderful. We get to talk about what's gonna happen today, what's bugging us

00:00:15.860 --> 00:00:21.620
It gives me time to think about big decisions, or new ideas, or just sing songs to myself

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.160
Or out loud - Whatever!

00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:26.180
Every morning there's a different song in my head.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:28.360
And I find this to be true all the time, actually.

00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:33.120
Pink!, Rocky Horror, Lamb Chop,  Matchbox Twenty. Always! There's always one there!

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:37.500
Why is that? Why is my brain set up for there to always be a song in it?

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.460
Just waiting for me to like, check it, and see what is it right now? Oh! Bonnie Raitt!

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:44.760
(Singing) "Let's give 'em something to talk about!"

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:50.160
Anyway, I really like doing this thing. It has made my life noticeably better, I'm less stressed out,

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:52.020
And the sunrises can be pretty great.

00:00:52.060 --> 00:00:57.840
But every morning when I get out of bed to put my long underwear on and jump into the frigid, pre-dawn Montana air,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:04.100
There is nothing in the world that I want to do more than get back into that warm, soft bed!

00:01:04.100 --> 00:01:10.180
I live an amazingly pampered life - there are hundreds of people all around my town who will,

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:13.640
For a small fee, make food for me, and then clean up after me!

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:19.840
There are several different holes in my house that hot water falls out of, whenever I want it to!

00:01:19.840 --> 00:01:25.460
And for the last 8 years or so, I've had a job that allows me to get out of bed whenever I want.

00:01:25.460 --> 00:01:28.980
And so I have slept in the majority of those days.

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:34.400
But I have pretty good evidence that staying in bed does not actually make me happier, or feel better.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:36.540
So every single morning, the question is pretty pressing:

00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:41.160
Do I do the thing that will make me happy right now, or the thing that will make me happier in the long term?

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:45.220
Not even that long term, really; we're talking like, like 20 minutes from now.

00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:50.660
And remarkably, it's really hard to do the thing that will make me happier 20 minutes from now,

00:01:50.740 --> 00:01:56.420
And for the entire rest of the day. Because "me" now doesn't care about "me" 20 minutes from now.

00:01:56.420 --> 00:01:58.120
I just wanna get back into bed!

00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:02.300
I've also been thinking about this ever since I made that video about vegetarianism, and how I am not a vegetarian

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:04.660
Despite the fact that I should be, and I know I should be.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:12.180
I've gotten a lot of messages saying "Dude! Suck it up! Dumbledore said it himself: you gotta choose between what is right, and what is easy"

00:02:12.180 --> 00:02:13.160
Or something like that.

00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:18.600
And I feel ya, vegetarians, who were mostly very nice... and sometimes not at all.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:24.820
I have no scientific evidence for this, but sometimes I feel like you can only do so many things you don't want to do

00:02:25.480 --> 00:02:28.340
Before you just accidentally eat a whole ice cream cake.

00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:34.280
I am amazed by some people's ability to do hard things all day long, forever.

00:02:34.380 --> 00:02:38.520
Particularly parents - I don't know how this happens.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.100
I'm amazed by you.

00:02:40.100 --> 00:02:43.400
But it's hard to do the hard thing! That's why they call it the hard thing.

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:45.800
And it's harder for some people to do the hard thing than others!

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:48.400
And it's harder at some times than other times.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:52.940
Like I've been having sad times lately,  despite the fact that there's gonna be a new Harry Potter book

00:02:52.940 --> 00:02:59.080
And also we've confirmed the existence of gravitational waves, which are like 2 of the Hankiest good news-es ever.

00:02:59.080 --> 00:03:03.220
And I'm not even going to talk about why I've been having sad times, because it's too sad, so I'm gonna put it in the description

00:03:03.300 --> 00:03:07.480
But I do know that what I should do are the things that help me do the hard thing more.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.980
Showing myself every morning that I'm happier because  I did a thing I didn't wanna do.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:16.620
Working on my ability to consciously be having a  positive effect on myself

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:20.700
And also on the people and the world around me is really important.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.480
And I always wanna be driving toward that.

00:03:22.480 --> 00:03:24.640
But I also don't wanna hate myself when I mess up.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:28.800
And I have no tips for how to not do the easy thing in any given moment

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:34.360
Except to just do it, and not let your conscious mind get too caught up in that decision.

00:03:34.360 --> 00:03:37.200
Because man! It's good at rationalizing and being like,

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:42.960
"You know you can go back to bed. Don't worry about it, just, you can get up in about 15 more minutes"

00:03:43.080 --> 00:03:44.400
By which I mean two and a half hours!

00:03:44.480 --> 00:03:47.600
Just jump into that cold pool of that thing you don't wanna do.

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.440
And if you can't, don't be too hard on yourself.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:51.920
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

